## Why
scen-check/scenario_quality failed: "E2E-001: subjective — 'Then step asserts
"Ada feels welcomed by what the greeter prints" — a human emotional state
with no stated expected output, so two reviewers can disagree on the same
printed text'". The user settled what counts as correct: a line matching
`^Hello Ada$` — the configured greeting, one space, the name, nothing else.
The two changes below state that same behaviour as an outcome a reviewer
settles by comparison, and keep the `then:` step an instance of the product
document's `then:` concept `standard output` ("A line the command printed on
its standard output has a match for a stated pattern, a regular
expression.", terms: command, standard output).

## Required Changes

